## Model card

- **Name:** Neomorph (unverified, claimed OpenCode Zen experimental model)
- **Short description:** Nothing publicly verifiable. The folder's `meta.json` claims an "OpenCode Zen experimental model (64K ctx, $0.50/$1.50) with modular sub-network architecture and structured-output focus". No such model appears on the live OpenCode Zen catalog, in models.dev, or in any public launch/docs surface found this pass.
- **Provider / access:** claimed: OpenCode Zen (`opencode/neomorph`, $0.50/$1.50 per 1M in/out). Verified: **absent** — live Zen `/v1/models` (86 entries, checked 2026-11-13) has no neomorph; models.dev full catalog (checked 2026-11-13) has no neomorph provider/model entry. "Neomorph" on the public web resolves only to a biotech (molecular glue degraders), game plugins and biology terms.
- **Release / knowledge:** claimed (experimental); undated and unverifiable.
- **IDs:** `opencode/neomorph` (claimed; not present in the live catalog).
- **Context window:** claimed 64,000 total / 4,096 max output (meta.json only).
- **Modalities:** claimed text in/out (meta.json only).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-13):** claimed $0.50/$1.50 per 1M (meta.json only; "provider documentation" link not found anywhere).
- **Architecture:** claimed "modular sub-network architecture" (meta.json only) — unverifiable.

